# chezmoi modify_ template for ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc.
# Rendered by chezmoi (Go template) into a Python merge script, then run with the
# current file on stdin; the merged result is emitted on stdout. Merge-only and
# idempotent across repeated `chezmoi apply` runs.
#
# opencode.jsonc is JSONC and its comments are load-bearing (the per-plugin
# supply-chain audit and permission rationale), so this follows
# dot_codex/modify_private_config.toml.tmpl and does
# LINE-LEVEL surgery. It never json.loads/json.dumps the target: a round trip
# through the json module would silently delete every comment in the file.
#
# Ownership boundary:
#   OWNED  - re-asserted on every apply: the file header comment, "$schema", V2
#            "plugins", and only agents.build.color / agents.plan.color. Every
#            other agent field, nested comment, and custom agent is preserved.
#            The retired singular "plugin" key is removed when present.
#   SEEDED - native "permissions" are written only when the incoming file has no
#            permission policy. The exact old seed is migrated; any customized
#            V1 "permission" or V2 "permissions" policy is preserved verbatim.
#   KEPT   - copied through verbatim, comments included: every other top-level
#            key, in its original order. That is how machine-local "instructions"
#            and "mcp" entries live in the target file without ever reaching the
#            public dotfiles repo.
#
# Comment attachment: a `//` run directly above a key (no blank line between)
# belongs to that key and moves or dies with it. Separate a comment from the key
# below it with a blank line if you want it treated as free-standing.
#
# Safety: if the incoming file is non-empty but cannot be walked as a
# line-oriented JSONC object (no root object, or a top-level key that does not
# start its own line), the input is emitted unchanged and a warning goes to
# stderr. Never destroy a hand-edited target, never block the rest of the apply.
#
# There is no component gate in here; the file is gated wholesale in
# home/.chezmoiignore under ai > opencode. It stays a .tmpl for parity with the
# other modify_ scripts and to render agent colors from the shared palette.
